  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD Strategic Peace building workshop, Goma, North Kivu, DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Great Lakes countries where CAFOD works for a decade is a theatre of conflict recurrence. These conflicts are either between communities within a country or between two countries accusing each other. Wanting to make an active contribution in the search for a lasting solution, CAFOD would launch a peace building programme which will include partners from the three countries of the Great Lakes region which are Burundi, DRC and Rwanda. Before the launch of this programme planned for April 2013, CAFOD is organizing a workshop with potential partners to determine the intervention strategy, relevant activities to implement and the main objectives. This is intended to expand the project proposal that CAFOD has already put in place and finally understand the dynamics of conflict in the region guarantee for a good response. 
Planned to be implemented internally by CAFOD with strong participation of potential partners from great lakes region, the peace building workshop will cost about 18,907 Usd to cover all cost (transport, accommodation, food, stationary, etc.).</narrative>
  </description>
